onale rests on a false characterization of the out-of-scope consumer.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd5fe2fa2875438a5","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Problem section, parenthetical on the Gerrit path","norm_id":"nde65730beab054a4","priority":0.68,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader relying on the plan's premise assumes the Gerrit path is already priority-aware and defers a needed fix to the sibling ticket that in fact must ADD the read."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Reword to: the Gerrit path (`adapter.py::_translate_findings`) does NOT yet carry `priority` — the sibling ticket patriotic-abdicative-arrowana adds it there; this ticket is scoped to the `review_result`/`review_code()` consumer only.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the fallback in _to_common_finding when a source finding lacks `priority`/`decision` (e.g. `f.get(\"priority\", 0.0)` / omit the key vs. a documented default), and add an AC/test covering a finding missing these keys.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0333,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: priority/decision are 'set on DET-tier findings by the sibling priority-backfill ticket' — i.e. not guaranteed present when this ticket lands","shim.py:55 _to_common_finding reads a plain dict via f.get(...) with no priority/decision handling today","AC line 1 requires the keys 'for every finding' but the source may not carry them"],"finding":"The plan does not specify the fallback when a source kernel finding lacks `priority` or `decision`. The plan itself notes DET-tier findings only acquire these via a SIBLING backfill ticket, so at this shim's read site a finding may be missing the keys — but no default/omission behavior is specified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2abdf45847c8aa4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('or set on DET-tier findings by the sibling priority-backfill ticket'); AC line 1 ('for every finding')","norm_id":"n3e2235c5da460ae8","priority":0.6667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["This ticket lands before the sibling backfill ticket; a DET-tier finding reaches the shim with no priority/decision key","A legacy/older kernel finding dict omits priority/decision"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Use `f.get(\"priority\", 0.0)` and `f.get(\"decision\")` (omitting the key when absent), and assert the missing-key case in the strengthened test so the 'for every finding' guarantee holds before the sibling backfill ticket lands.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the value vocabulary of the `priority` key added to the common finding (float 0..1, higher=more important, = kernel validity×impact) and disambiguate it from common.schema.json's existing 0..4 ticket-`priority` $def — either name it distinctly (e.g. `kernel_priority`) or document the two senses in the schema.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["common.schema.json #/$defs/priority: {type:integer, minimum:0, maximum:4, '0=critical … 4=backlog (default 2)'}","decide.py:681 `priority = round(val * imp, 4)` — a float, higher=worse","common.finding has additionalProperties:true, so the collision is not caught by validation","Plan Problem: 'the numeric priority (validity x impact)'"],"finding":"The plan adds a `priority` key to the common `finding` whose value is the kernel's validity×impact float, but common.schema.json already defines a `priority` $def with a contradictory vocabulary (integer 0..4, '0=critical … 4=backlog', lower=worse). The plan never defines the type/range/direction of the finding.priority it introduces, so a review_result consumer cannot tell which `priority` sense applies.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd1f1933c4c0ea1f7","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach; AC line 1 ('includes `priority` … in its output dict')","norm_id":"n85c